d \"aniridia\" in \"people with aniridia.\" I'm now carefully computing character offsets for each of these by counting through the text letter by letter to pin down exact start and end positions.\n\n", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "{\"annotations\":[{\"start\":48,\"end\":63,\"text\":\"simple aniridia\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Names a specific defined condition (uncomplicated aniridia) in the title; it is not a family of diseases and needs no gene or organism anchor.\",\"guideline_section\":\"Section 1 - What to Annotate: Specific Disease / Disease Class\"},{\"start\":121,\"end\":129,\"text\":\"aniridia\",\"entity\":\"Modifier\",\"rationale\":\"The disease term 'aniridia' directly premodifies the clinical head 'patients', so the ordinary Modifier rule applies rather than the molecular-head rule.\",\"guideline_section\":\"Section 3 - Modifiers (disease mentions used as modifiers; negative constraint b for clinical heads)\"},{\"start\":279,\"end\":287,\"text\":\"aniridia\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Used as the standalone referent of the prepositional phrase 'people with aniridia', denoting the specific condition under study rather than premodifying another noun.\",\"guideline_section\":\"Section 1 - What to Annotate: Specific Disease / Disease Class\"}]}", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 9652, "output_tokens": 6622, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 6236}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}